===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pekʷ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|cook}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cōc|t=a cook}}, from {{der|en|la|cocus}}, ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*pekʷ-|t=to cook, become ripe}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nds|kokk}}, {{cog|nl|kok}}, {{cog|de|Koch}}, {{cog|da|kok}}, {{cog|no|kokk}}, {{cog|sv|kock}}, {{cog|is|kokkur|t=cook}}. Also compare {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kokōn|t=to cook}}.

