#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Pal Benko|title=Endgame Lab|magazine=w:Chess Life|location=New Windsor, N.Y.|publisher=w:United States Chess Federation|month=June|year=2003|volume=58|issue=6|page=49|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_chess-life_2003-06_58_6/page/49/mode/1up|issn=0197-260X|oclc=5885790|passage=The original endgame was one file to the right (Kf1, Kb5 etc.). But there is a '''cook''' after 1. c6 dxc6 2. d6 cxd6 3. h4 gxh3 e.p. 4. gxh3 Ka4! 5. h4 b5. My version eliminates the '''cook'''.}}

