===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pekʷ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|coken}}, from the noun {{m|en|cook}}. In the slang sense of "proceed with some plan", {{coinage|en|Q5951242|in=2010|nocap=1}} and popularized in viral tweets and TikToks in mid-2022.<ref>{{R:KYM|Let Him Cook / Let That Boy Cook|https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/let-him-cook-let-that-boy-cook}}</ref>

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|prepare food}} {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[prepare]] [[food]] for [[eat]]ing by [[heat]]ing it, often [[combine|combining]] with other [[ingredients]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''cooking''' bangers and mash.}}
#: {{ux|en|He's in the kitchen, '''cooking'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date= 27 October 2015|page=192|title= The Simple Secrets to Cooking Everything Better|author=w:Matt Preston|publisher= Plum|url= https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=zMaDCgAAQBAJ |isbn= 9781845698232 |passage=  You could just use ordinary shop-bought kecap manis to marinade the meat, but making your own is easy, has a far more elegant fragrance and is, above all, such a great brag! Flavouring kecap manis is an intensely personal thing, so try this version now and next time '''cook''' the sauce down with crushed, split lemongrass and a shredded lime leaf.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be cooked.
#: {{ux|en|The dinner is '''cooking''' on the stove.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively}} To be [[uncomfortably]] [[hot]].
#: {{syn|en|bake|stew}}
#: {{ux|en|Look at that poor dog shut up in that car on a day like today - it must be '''cooking''' in there.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[kill]], [[destroy]], or otherwise [[render]] [[useless]] or [[inoperative]] through [[exposure]] to [[excessive]] [[heat]] or [[radiation]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Randall Munroe|chapter=Periodic Wall of the Elements|title={{w|What If? (book)|What If?}}|location=New York, New York|publisher=w:Houghton Mifflin Harcourt|year=2014|page=41|isbn=978-0-544-27299-6|text=You would die from what we might call "extremely acute radiation poisoning" – that is, you would be '''cooked'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Howard Tayler|work=w:Schlock Mercenary|date=6 July 2017|url=https://www.schlockmercenary.com/2017-07-06|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240120160638/https://www.schlockmercenary.com/2017-07-06|archivedate=20 January 2024|accessdate=20 January 2024|text="What's coming?"  "Dunno yet.  ''Cindy!''  Active scanning!  Pulse hard, but don't '''cook''' any friendlies."  "We have sensors that can '''cook''' people?"  "Another reason why warship combat is not an indoor sport."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[execute]] by [[electric chair]].
#: {{syn|en|fry}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|military slang}} To [[hold on]] to a [[grenade]] [[briefly]] after [[ignite|igniting]] the [[fuse]], so that it [[explode]]s [[almost]] [[immediately]] after being [[throw]]n.
#: {{syn|en|cook off}}
#: {{ux|en|I always '''cook''' my [[frag]]s, in case they try to grab one and throw it back.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[concoct]] or [[prepare]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Frank Spalding|title=Methamphetamine: The Dangers of Crystal Meth|page=47|passage=The process of '''cooking''' meth can leave residue on surfaces all over the home, exposing all of its occupants to the drug.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[tamper]] with or [[alter]]; to [[cook up]].
